prompt:
Use case: identity-preserve.
Create a real six-frame illustrated tiny happy hop animation of Cecilia, in her approved travel cloak costume. Reference 1 is the classic hop choreography only; redraw the complete figures wearing reference 2's approved travel costume and identity. References 3 and 4 confirm the established chibi rendering and mint-green hair/green eyes; reference 5 is the official episode-05 cloak clothing evidence, not the adult body proportions.
Costume in ALL SIX figures: bare mint-green hair with no saint veil, raspberry red hooded short cape with burgundy trim, white collar blouse, narrow blue ribbon tie, dark navy pleated skirt with simple clean hem (NO saint lace), dark stockings and navy shoes. Preserve identical large head, petite 2.5-head body, delicate anime linework and soft cel shading from the approved travel canonical.
Exactly TWO ROWS × THREE separated whole characters, top row left-to-right then bottom row left-to-right. Every full actor is independently drawn, same head size and same physical proportions. Keep ample empty transparent row gap and side gutters.
Pose order:
1 grounded calm happy stance, little excited hands near chest;
2 slight anticipatory knee crouch, smiling green eyes;
3 tiny takeoff, both shoes off the common floor, knees gently folded, small fists near chest;
4 apex with closed happy smiling eyes, both feet airborne and tucked, hands near shoulders, gentle compact cape and hair follow-through;
5 landing, both soles grounded, knees bending as the cape/hair settle;
6 same calm grounded stance as frame 1.
The hop is tiny: head crown should rise only about 1–2% of the standing height; folding the knees makes shoes at apex 8–12% above the common floor. No huge leap or splayed pose. Standing figures must keep full canonical physical height; do not shrink entire characters into compressed bodies. Standing head crown and body proportions remain identical in frames 1 and 6.
Landscape 3:2 canvas. All grounded shoes share a row baseline at approximately 86% of each row height. Airborne shoes retain true lift above that baseline. Complete hair/cape/feet inside every cell; character width stays under 90% of standing character height so extraction will not shrink standing figures. Long hair gently waves with compact ends, do not spread into a wide horizontal fan.
Truly transparent RGBA background. No stage, floor shadow, ground line, sparkles, effects, motion marks, dust, blur, text, numbers, borders, props, or other people. Six complete separated drawings only.
